# The Elemental Trials - Game Introduction
# A complete showcase of cutscene features: backdrops, transitions, BGM, SFX, portraits, and animations

@backdrop textures/room.gif [fadeIn=1200]
@char HERO sprite=characters/male
@char ELDER sprite=characters/female
@char KNIGHT sprite=npc/air-knight

# Start with dramatic opening music
@do playBgm [name=audio/opening.mp3]

wait 1500

# Scene 1: A Peaceful Morning

*HERO: [cutin=size=large,expression=neutral]
"""
Another peaceful day in the village...
The sun rises over the mountains.
"""

wait 800

@transition wipe [duration=600]

wait 500

@backdrop textures/forest.gif [fadeIn=800]

HERO: [expression=smile,position=left]
"""
Time to check on the village elder.
She mentioned something important yesterday.
"""

wait 1000

# Dramatic sound effect
@do playSfx [name=audio/organ.mp3]

@transition fadeOutBackdrop [duration=400]

wait 600

# Scene 2: The Elder's Warning

@backdrop textures/cave.gif [fadeIn=700]
@do playBgm [name=audio/distorted-communication.mp3]

ELDER: [expression=worried,position=right]
"""
Hero! Thank the heavens you've arrived!
Dark omens cloud my visions...
"""

wait 600

HERO: [expression=shocked,position=left] What troubles you, Elder?

*ELDER: [cutin=size=large,expression=worried]
"""
The Four Elemental Guardians have awakened!
Fire, Water, Earth, and Air...
They guard the seal that binds the Dark Lord!
"""

wait 800

HERO: [expression=worried,position=left]
"""
The Dark Lord? But the legends say...
He was defeated a thousand years ago!
"""

ELDER: [expression=neutral,position=right]
"""
Defeated, yes. Destroyed? No.
The seal weakens with each passing century.
Only a hero who conquers all four trials...
"""

wait 600

*ELDER: [cutin=size=large,expression=neutral]
"""
...may renew the seal and save our world!
You are our only hope, young warrior.
"""

@do playSfx [name=audio/dungeon-beat.mp3]

wait 1000

@transition wipe [duration=500]

wait 600

# Scene 3: The Knight's Guidance

@backdrop textures/castle.gif [fadeIn=800]
@do playBgm [name=audio/brass-loop.mp3]

KNIGHT: [expression=neutral,position=right]
"""
Greetings, chosen one.
I am the Guardian Knight of the Elemental Gates.
"""

wait 500

HERO: [expression=neutral,position=left] The Elder sent me. I'm ready for the trials.

*KNIGHT: [cutin=size=large,expression=neutral]
"""
Your courage is admirable!
But courage alone won't suffice.
Listen well to my guidance...
"""

wait 800

KNIGHT: [expression=neutral,position=right]
"""
FIRE burns in the northwest - raw power!
WATER flows in the northeast - adaptability!
EARTH stands in the southwest - endurance!
AIR soars in the southeast - agility!
"""

wait 1000

HERO: [expression=smile,position=left]
"""
I understand. Four trials, four elements.
Each teaching a different virtue.
"""

KNIGHT: [expression=neutral,position=right]
"""
Correct! Collect all four Elemental Shards.
Only then will the path to the Dark Lord open.
"""

wait 800

*HERO: [cutin=size=large,expression=smile]
"""
I won't let anyone down!
For the village, for the kingdom...
For everyone I love!
"""

@do playBgm [name=audio/dawns-peak.mp3]

wait 1000

@transition fadeOutBackdrop [duration=800]

wait 600

# Scene 4: The Journey Begins

@backdrop textures/temple.gif [fadeIn=900]

wait 600

ELDER: [expression=smile,position=left]
"""
May the spirits of the ancients guide you.
Return to us victorious, hero!
"""

KNIGHT: [expression=neutral,position=right]
"""
The portals await you in the dungeon entrance.
Each leads to an elemental chamber.
"""

wait 800

HERO: [expression=neutral,position=center]
"""
Then my journey begins now.
Watch over the village while I'm gone.
"""

*HERO: [cutin=size=large,expression=smile]
"""
When I return...
The Dark Lord will never threaten us again!
"""

wait 1000

@do playBgm [name=audio/calm-escape.mp3]

@transition wipe [duration=700]

wait 800

@backdrop textures/room.gif [fadeIn=600]

wait 500

KNIGHT: [expression=neutral,position=center]
"""
And so the hero's journey begins...
May fortune favor the brave.
"""

wait 1500

@transition fadeOutBackdrop [duration=1000]

waitInput

@end
